Add web research and content drafting

Research
- research_web runs a SEPARATE, ISOLATED agent loop with only two tools, both
  web-facing: web_search and fetch_page. It has no database access and no
  proposal tools, so injected instructions inside a fetched page cannot reach
  anything that writes. Web pages are attacker-controlled text, and an agent that
  can both read an arbitrary page and write to the store is the dangerous
  combination this design has avoided throughout.
- _shared/web.ts does the retrieval: plain GET with a timeout, a 500 kB response
  cap, markup stripped to text, and every result explicitly labelled untrusted.
- Search uses DuckDuckGo's HTML endpoint, so no API key and no vendor lock-in.
  Failures are reported as clear messages rather than an empty list, which would
  otherwise look like "nothing exists".

Content drafting
- propose_blog_post creates or updates a Wisdom Vault article. New posts default
  to unpublished drafts; publishing requires an explicit request. Slug collisions
  are refused with the conflicting title.
- propose_marketing_content saves newsletter, social and partner-outreach copy to
  marketing_drafts (new migration). The agent never sends anything: a message that
  leaves the building cannot be recalled, so sending stays a human action.
- Undo deletes created rows and restores updated ones.

Also fixes the registry declaration order, which had drifted again: the tool
registry is now declared once, after every tool object, with a comment explaining
why it must stay last.
